A||||19||MooCow||Camaro vs. Fiero||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||12-10-1999||10:37 PM||||Se my friend loves Camaro's and recently purchased a 1991 Camaro loaded.  I want a Fiero and plan on getting one in the spring.   The thing is which will be faster.  I want to find a little car that has as much pick up as a camaro and I hear that a Fiero does.   Is that true?  I want to be able to finally have a car with some balls that may be able to beat his 302 Camaro.        What do you all think?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||12-10-1999||10:53 PM||||A v6 Fiero in good condition should be able to hold it's own against that Camaro, and you have lots of options if you want more power.  Just do a search for "engine swaps"||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-11-1999||12:48 AM||||Well, this may be nitpicking, but if that 1991 Camaro has the original engine, it's a gutless 305, not the old manly Z-28 302.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||03:29 AM||||Yeah...Just over 200horses in a car that weighs at least 1000# more than ours.  A Fiero ought to handle better, too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||12-11-1999||04:50 AM||||In 91 the 305's had two types of injection systems.  One was the TBI rated at 170 hp and 255 lb-ft.  The TPI was rated at 220 hp and around 285 lb-ft of torque.  If the Fiero you buy comes with a manual you just might be able to beat your friends car if he has the TBI model.  I had a friend with the TBi and we both had auto tranny's and he beat me by a car up to about 70 or so.  If your freind has the TPI, you can forget about beating him unless his car is not running well.  305 TPI were capable of low 15 second times from the factory.  Stock to Stock the 305 will win everytime.<P>One thing you can do to definately beat him is to add nitrous to your fiero.<P>Some bolt ons that will help if you don't have or want nitrous would be a power pulley, porting the stock exhaust manifolds, a gutted cat and a high flow muffler, and if willing enough 1.6 rockers would be a good add on.  With these mods you should hang with a stock 305 TPI<P>Adding nitrous will take your freinds car for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||12-11-1999||11:18 AM||||Monkeyman,  <BR> A fiero "ought" to handle better than a camaro??!?  Have you ever been in one?  They handle like the family station wagon!  It's a big stupid car with all the weight up front. It also weighs a good 1000lbs more than a fiero.  My friend's brother bought a 6speed 5.7l trans-am (4th gen), and loved the power... but he said that on turns where he would do 70mph, the trans-am could only do it at 30mph!  And you didn't mention if he had the V8 or the V6!  Big difference.  You would eat the V6 alive with a GT 5speed.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||12-11-1999||11:46 AM||||Thanks for the reply's.  I believe that it is a TBI Camaro. Everything is stock auto matic.  So I guess I will just have to see what kind of Fiero I can get for about $4,000 in the spring. Thanks again. Ken||||reg||1
Z||000007||RFMike||12-11-1999||03:47 PM||||Shiner,<BR>I think your friend has exagerated about the cornering capabilities of the Trans Am.  About 30 mph worth.  The Fiero will beat the TA in cornering, but not by a factor of 2 1/3.<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||06:42 PM||||Shiner--I've never raced a Camaro, so I didn't want to stick my neck out too far.  I've done that before (many times here) and had it cut off! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||12-13-1999||09:53 AM||||Hey MooCow, if you just want to show up your friend for the afternoon, you're more than welcome to "borrow" my turbo-charged 86SE! This car is very fast, and often scares me! Myself I've never raced a camaro, but I did get into it with an early 90's vette. He had a head start, before I new it the vette was beside me, then behind me! I slammed on the brakes just in time for the next light! The driver of the vette wasn't very pleased. I couldn't stop laughing! You're budget of $4000 will buy you a nice GT, and anyone on this forum will be more than happy to help you find one! As always, I'll keep my eyes open!||||reg||1
Z||000010||DJRice||12-14-1999||09:02 AM||||Just make sure that you get a car that you are going to be happy with for a while, because no matter what you do, there will always be a car faster than yours.  Make sure that you can say "Hey man, good show" and still keep your head up just in case you end up looking at the Taillights.<P>Of course, thats no fun, but I'd hate to see someone get down on the car because its not the fastest thing on the road.  The Fieros are Quick, Nimble, and a whole lot of fun.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||10:59 AM||||It's like DJRice said...Be a good sport.  Don't think you're ever gonna beat one of the supercars.  I'm all for improving my Fiero, but no matter what I do, it'll never hang with the new Porsches, Ferarris, etc. (There are more of them around than you think! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  Let me give you my version of his last sentence:  Fieros may not be the quickest, nor the most nimble, but the *are* the most fun!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||loafer87gt||12-14-1999||12:21 PM||||I beleive all 87 and up Camaro's 305s are TPI. My buddy has an 88 IROC 305 and that thing can clean my clock after 100 kph. In short sprints up to a hundred its close, but after that, the cubic inches kick in and hes gone. I've always found Camaros and Firebirds kinda amusing. When I was little kid I can remember being on the school bus and a dude in a bandit style Trans Am pulled up next to us and  all the kids on the bus stared in awe. Now I look at a F-body and say to myself, oh look, theres a nice piece of crap.||||reg||1
Z||000013||86_Fastback||12-14-1999||04:49 PM||||loafer,<BR>Care to back up that staement about TAs? My 98 TA is faster and handles better than my 86 Fiero GT.  Facts are facts and numbers don't lie.  The fiero is fun as hell to drive, but performance is lacking compared to my TA.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||12-14-1999||05:39 PM||||The 305 was available as a TPI and TBI, up through '92 (I believe). I had an 88 Firebird Formula with the WS-6, 16" wheels, 5-speed, etc. It was a TBI. 170 H.P. Would *just about* get out of its own way, but that's all. Cornered like a slot car, rode like a buckboard wagon. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||12-14-1999||08:50 PM||||**sigh** I sure miss my old 77 Trans Am with a 400 (6.6L) engine, posi 3.73 rear end, and Super T-10 4 speed tranny. It didn't handle quite as good as a Fiero, but it flat out flew on the straights.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||09:58 PM||||86_Fastback-I'll bet you have the 350ci in you TA.  There's alot of difference between your motor and the previous gen 305.<P>batboy--ditto.  I had a '78 set up like yours.  I wish I still had mine, too, although it wasn't as much fun to drive as a Fiero!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fiero SE||12-14-1999||10:03 PM||||We have an 89 Trans Am 305 and it would be a close race with a Fiero V6... The Trans Am would most likely beat it but not by a whole lot. But with a few mods on the Fiero VS no mods ont the camaro, it would be close. ||||reg||10
Z||000018||sdm1964||12-14-1999||10:25 PM||||I have both an 85 GT and an 84 Z28. For all out horsepower the Z will win every time. For fun to drive and being different the GT wins. My Z28 is not a piece of crap. It is a solid built, Powerfull, stop on a dime and give you 5 cents change muscle car. Don't get me wrong, I really love my GT, but i will never get rid of my 305HO, 5 speed, red road rocket. I have the best of both worlds, A Z28 Camaro and Fiero GT.||||reg||6
Z||000019||HotFieroGT||12-15-1999||01:20 AM||||I used to have an 84 Z28 with the HO 305 (190HP) and an automatic.  I raced a buddy of mine who had an 86 GT at the time and we were always about the same.  I know if his Fiero had a 5 speed he could have beat me off the line but I think I could have beat him on the top end no matter what.  I still like my 88GT's better than any (Yawn) Camaro out there.  And I guarantee I get more looks than they do!<P>||||reg||12
